# Visual scripting conventions

- Keep graphs small and focused; extract repeated logic into Subgraphs (not SuperUnits)
- Use descriptive names for all variables and custom events
- Add sticky notes to explain complex logic
- Use State Graphs for AI, dialog systems, and game states
- Use Script Graphs for sequential gameplay logic
- Avoid deeply nested branches; prefer state machines for complex conditions
- Use Object variables for component references instead of repeated Find calls
- Create custom C# units for performance-critical operations
- Document graph inputs and outputs in the graph description field
- Use Script Machine component (not the legacy Flow Machine name)
